    "q-34164": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34164",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, then $-\\frac{1}{2}b=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying each component of $b$ by $-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}b & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
