    "q-73932": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73932",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\frac{1}{2}p-\\frac{1}{3}q.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply each component of $p$ by $\\frac{1}{2}$ and each component of $q$ by $\\frac{1}{3}.$ Then, we substract the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}p-\\frac{1}{3}q & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0-(-3) \\\\ 4-1 \\\\ -3-0 \\\\ 1-2 \\\\ 1-(-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-73932-a",
