    "q-73949": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73949",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Let $l=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ x \\\\ 2 \\\\ x \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}]$ and $m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $l\\cdot m=3$ and $x>3$, find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $l\\cdot m=3,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l\\cdot m & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot 1+x\\cdot x+2\\cdot 4+x\\cdot (-1)+2x\\cdot (-3) & =3 \\\\ 5+{x}^{2}+8-x-6x & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+13 & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>3$, our final answer is $x=5$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
