    "q-73948": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73948",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Let $v=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3x \\\\ -3 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $v\\cdot w=-2$ and $x>0$, find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $v\\cdot w=-2,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot w & =-2 \\\\ x\\cdot 3x+2x\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot 2 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6x+4x-10 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>0$, our final answer is $x=2$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
