    "q-35129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35129",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Let\n$a=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}p \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $a\\cdot b=8$, find the value of $p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $a\\cdot b=8,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $p$ and then solve for $p$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =8 \\\\ 5\\cdot p+0\\cdot (-3)+p\\cdot 7+1\\cdot (-4) & =8 \\\\ 5p+7p-4 & =8 \\\\ 12p & =12 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $p=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
